From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Subject: [PATCH] zink: MoltenVK's depth images without host transfer, at run time

zink already leaves VK_IMAGE_USAGE_HOST_TRANSFER_BIT_EXT off images on MoltenVK,
which cannot allocate a depth/stencil image with it (no memory type fits:
memoryTypeBits is 0), but only when MVK_VERSION is defined, so only when zink
is built against MoltenVK's headers. A Windows build running on Wine's Vulkan,
with MoltenVK under it, never is: every depth/stencil allocation failed, so
each WGL window's depth buffer was missing and the first wglMakeCurrent raised
GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY ("Resizing framebuffer"). Check the driver ID instead.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
index 678f455..35fa49b 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
@@ -605,12 +605,12 @@ check_ici(struct zink_screen *screen, VkImageCreateInfo *ici, uint64_t modifier)
       image_props = props2.imageFormatProperties;
       if (screen->info.have_EXT_host_image_copy && ici->usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_HOST_TRANSFER_BIT_EXT)
          optimalDeviceAccess = hic.optimalDeviceAccess;
-#if defined(MVK_VERSION)
       // MoltenVK cannot allocate a depth buffer with VK_IMAGE_USAGE_HOST_TRANSFER_BIT_EXT
       // As hic.identicalMemoryLayout is set, it is not needed?
-      if (screen->info.have_EXT_host_image_copy && ici->usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_HOST_TRANSFER_BIT_EXT && hic.identicalMemoryLayout)
+      // Checked at run time: on Windows (Wine's Vulkan) MoltenVK is the driver without its headers.
+      if (screen->info.driver_props.driverID == VK_DRIVER_ID_MOLTENVK &&
+          screen->info.have_EXT_host_image_copy && ici->usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_HOST_TRANSFER_BIT_EXT && hic.identicalMemoryLayout)
          optimalDeviceAccess = false;
-#endif
    } else
       ret = VKSCR(GetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties)(screen->pdev, ici->format, ici->imageType,
                                                    ici->tiling, ici->usage, ici->flags, &image_props);
